  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice has scored XXX marks in her test and Bob has scored YYY marks in the same test. Alice is happy if she scored at least twice the marks of Bob’s score. Determine whether she is happy or not.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains two space-separated integers X,YX, YX,Y — the marks of Alice and Bob respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, print `Yes` if Alice is happy and `No` if she is not, according to the problem statement.\n\n\nThe judge is case insensitive so you may output the answer in any case. In particular `YES`, `yes`, yEs`are all considered equivalent to`Yes`.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y≤1001 \\leq X, Y \\leq 1001≤X,Y≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 1",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAlice has scored X=2X = 2X=2 marks whereas Bob has scored Y=1Y = 1Y=1 mark. As Alice has scored twice as much as Bob (i.e. X≥2YX \\geq 2YX≥2Y), the answer is Yes."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 2",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAlice has scored X=1X = 1X=1 mark whereas Bob has scored Y=2Y = 2Y=2 marks. As Alice has not scored twice as much as Bob (i.e. X<2YX \\lt 2YX<2Y), the answer is No."
      }
    ]
  },
